From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UebelAndre <github@uebelandre.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:31:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ide): go to the targets a macro defines in the same file

A label inside a macro usually names a target the macro itself creates,
often from its arguments: `deps = [":" + name + "_lib"]` next to
`native.cc_library(name = name + "_lib")`. Resolving such a label as a
BUILD target found nothing (and jumped to the top of the BUILD file),
since those names only exist once the macro runs.

Go to definition now first looks for a call in the same file whose
`name` argument builds the same name, comparing literal pieces and the
source of expression pieces: plain strings, `+` chains, `%` templates,
`.format()` templates, and `"//" + native.package_name() + ":..."`
prefixes. Calls in the function enclosing the cursor win over calls
elsewhere in the file. Labels into other packages or repositories are
left to the existing resolution.
